sibling nests: the range of the shared symbol is the hull of both bindings: true
sibling nests: the shared symbol has exactly one entry: true
inner siblings: the range of the shared symbol is the hull of both bindings: true
inner siblings: the enclosing loop keeps its own range: true
inner siblings: one entry per symbol: true
of_bindings hulls in either order: true
bind widens an existing range: true
a symbol no loop binds has no range: true
an access-validity query ranged by loop_ranges sees the second sibling's out-of-bounds cells: true
the same query over the first sibling's range alone admits the access (the hull is what decides): true
